{"subjectId":"cpp","id":"modern-cpp-tour","title":"Modern C++ Feature Tour (11 → 23)","group":"Modern C++ & Interview Prep","order":75,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">A quick map of what each standard added, with the features you'll actually use and be asked about.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-number-11\"></i>C++11 — the big one</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;memory&gt;\n#include &lt;unordered_map&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\nenum class Color { Red, Green };                             // scoped enums\n\nint main() {\n    auto v = std::vector&lt;int&gt;{1, 2, 3};                      // auto + brace init\n    for (auto x : v) std::cout &lt;&lt; x;                         // range-for\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    auto p = std::shared_ptr&lt;int&gt;(new int(7));               // smart pointers\n    std::unordered_map&lt;int, int&gt; m{{1, 1}};                  // hash containers\n    int* none = nullptr;                                     // nullptr\n    auto sq = [](int x) { return x * x; };                   // lambdas\n    static_assert(sizeof(int) &gt;= 4);                         // static_assert\n    constexpr int k = 3;                                     // constexpr\n    std::vector&lt;std::unique_ptr&lt;int&gt;&gt; owners;\n    owners.push_back(std::make_unique&lt;int&gt;(1));              // move semantics (make_unique is C++14)\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; *p + sq(k) + m[1] + (none == nullptr) + *owners[0] &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    Color c = Color::Green;\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; static_cast&lt;int&gt;(c) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>123\n19\n1</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Standard</th><th>Language</th><th>Library</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>C++11</strong></td><td><code>auto</code>, <code>decltype</code>, lambdas, rvalue refs &amp; move, <code>nullptr</code>, <code>constexpr</code>, range-for, <code>enum class</code>, <code>override</code>/<code>final</code>, variadic templates, <code>= default</code>/<code>= delete</code>, uniform init, <code>noexcept</code></td><td><code>unique_ptr</code>/<code>shared_ptr</code>, <code>unordered_*</code>, <code>thread</code>/<code>mutex</code>/<code>atomic</code>, <code>chrono</code>, <code>random</code>, <code>tuple</code>, <code>array</code>, <code>function</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>C++14</strong></td><td>Generic lambdas, return-type deduction, relaxed <code>constexpr</code>, binary literals, digit separators <code>1'000</code></td><td><code>make_unique</code>, <code>std::exchange</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>C++17</strong></td><td>Structured bindings, <code>if constexpr</code>, <code>if (init; cond)</code>, fold expressions, CTAD, inline variables, guaranteed copy elision, nested namespaces</td><td><code>optional</code>, <code>variant</code>, <code>any</code>, <code>string_view</code>, <code>filesystem</code>, parallel algorithms, <code>gcd</code>/<code>lcm</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>C++20</strong></td><td>Concepts, <code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, designated initialisers, <code>consteval</code>/<code>constinit</code>, coroutines, modules, <code>using enum</code>, lambda templates</td><td>Ranges, <code>format</code>, <code>span</code>, <code>jthread</code>, <code>stop_token</code>, <code>latch</code>/<code>barrier</code>/<code>semaphore</code>, calendar &amp; time zones, <code>contains()</code>, <code>starts_with()</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>C++23</strong></td><td>Deducing <code>this</code>, <code>if consteval</code>, multidimensional <code>operator[]</code>, <code>auto(x)</code> decay copy</td><td><code>print</code>/<code>println</code>, <code>expected</code>, <code>ranges::to</code>, <code>views::zip/enumerate/chunk</code>, <code>flat_map</code>, <code>mdspan</code>, <code>stacktrace</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-sparkles\"></i>C++17 &amp; C++20 in one program</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;algorithm&gt;\n#include &lt;compare&gt;\n#include &lt;concepts&gt;\n#include &lt;format&gt;\n#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;map&gt;\n#include &lt;optional&gt;\n#include &lt;ranges&gt;\n#include &lt;span&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\nstruct Version {\n    int major{}, minor{};\n    auto operator&lt;=&gt;(const Version&amp;) const = default;           // C++20 spaceship\n};\n\nstd::optional&lt;int&gt; parse(std::string_view s) {                 // C++17 optional + string_view\n    int n = 0;\n    for (char c : s) { if (c &lt; '0' || c &gt; '9') return std::nullopt; n = n * 10 + (c - '0'); }\n    return n;\n}\n\nstd::integral auto total(std::span&lt;const int&gt; xs) {            // C++20 concepts + span\n    int s = 0;\n    for (int x : xs) s += x;\n    return s;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::map&lt;std::string, Version&gt; deps{{\"fmt\", {.major = 10, .minor = 1}}, {\"boost\", {1, 84}}};  // designated init\n    for (const auto&amp; [name, ver] : deps)                                                          // structured bindings\n        std::cout &lt;&lt; std::format(\"{:&lt;6}{}.{}\\n\", name, ver.major, ver.minor);                     // std::format\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; (Version{1, 84} &lt; Version{10, 1}) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; nums{5, 3, 8};\n    std::ranges::sort(nums);                                                                      // ranges\n    if (auto n = parse(\"42\"); n) std::cout &lt;&lt; *n + total(nums) &lt;&lt; '\\n';                           // if-init\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; deps.contains(\"fmt\") &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>boost 1.84\nfmt   10.1\n1\n58\n1</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list\"></i>Features to know by name</h3>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-player-pause\"></i>Coroutines (C++20)</h3><p>Functions that can suspend (<code>co_await</code>, <code>co_yield</code>, <code>co_return</code>). The language provides the machinery; you need a library type (e.g. C++23 <code>std::generator</code>) to use them comfortably.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-packages\"></i>Modules (C++20)</h3><p><code>import std;</code> / <code>export module math;</code> replace textual <code>#include</code>: faster builds, no macro leakage. Toolchain support is still maturing.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-circle-check\"></i><code>std::expected</code> (C++23)</h3><p>Return a value <em>or</em> an error without exceptions: <code>std::expected&lt;int, std::string&gt; parse(...)</code>.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-back-up\"></i>Deducing <code>this</code> (C++23)</h3><p><code>void f(this auto&amp; self)</code> — one member function for const/non-const, recursive lambdas, CRTP without templates.</p></div></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What were the most important changes in C++11?</summary><div><p>Move semantics and rvalue references (cheap transfers of resources), smart pointers (safe ownership), lambdas, <code>auto</code>, range-based for, a memory model with <code>std::thread</code>/atomics, <code>nullptr</code>, <code>constexpr</code>, <code>enum class</code>, <code>override</code>/<code>final</code> and variadic templates. Together they made “modern C++” — code without manual <code>new</code>/<code>delete</code>.</p></div></details></section>"}